#!/bin/bash
#PBS -N cgm_push
#PBS -P 11704243
#PBS -j oe
#   qsub -l select=1:ncpus=8:mem=32gb -l walltime=00:30:00 \
#        -o logs/98_push_report.log scripts/pbs/98_push_report.pbs            # -> qdev
source "${REPO:-$HOME/workspace/Project_CGM/CGM-OutlierMIA-master}/scripts/pbs/env.sh"
set +e
module load git/2.39.2
cd "$REPO"
{
  git add -A
  echo "staged: $(git diff --cached --numstat | wc -l) files"
  git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'
Seven-day: the question was asked of a model that could not answer it

The h96 seven-day pilot was written off behind a quality gate reading 0.9475. That
number was one draw of an unseeded classifier: quality.discriminative_score seeded the
subsample and the batch draw but not the GRU's weight initialisation, so a score
depended on how many models had been evaluated earlier in the same process. The same
byte-identical samples.npy reads 0.9475, 0.5908 and 0.6483.

Fixed, and redone as a distribution -- eight restarts, fixed subsample, only the
initialisation moving:

                             min    median    max    spread
  copy_paste, 7 days       0.4950   0.5067  0.5100   0.0150
  h256, 7 days, 22k        0.4875   0.5242  0.5508   0.0633
  h96,  7 days, 34k        0.4792   0.6383  0.8442   0.3650
  h96,  7 days, 22k        0.4967   0.5538  0.9883   0.4917

h96 kept every checkpoint, so its own checkpoint-11 is the same 22,000 steps h256 was
read at. At matched steps the narrow model is separable at 0.988 and the wide one is
not. Width is the whole story, and over-training is excluded because h96 is MORE
separable at 22k than at 34k.

So "longer windows" was not a dead end -- it was untested. The copy_paste ceiling
result stands separately; that measurement never involved DiM-TS. The 21-model pilot is
re-running at hidden_size 256, 22,000 steps, 139 GPU.h, ETA 2026-08-19.

The instability has structure worth keeping: where a generator is genuinely
indistinguishable the classifier lands at chance every time (spread 0.015-0.06); where
a separable feature exists the draws are bimodal (spread 0.37-0.49). Report the maximum
over restarts, not one draw. That caveat is now attached to the three-channel quality
figures and the width sweep, whose direction holds but whose size was measured the old
way.

Also in this commit: the two-channel pilot relaunched at 40,000 steps after its own
loss trace showed convergence by 20k; the walltime arithmetic that killed the
three-channel campaign and was about to cost the two-channel pilot five models is now
an executable assertion inside the job; docs/PITFALLS.md 16; HISTORY stage 14;
SUMMARY_CN revised to 2026-08-18.

check_report_data.py re-derives 125 of the page's numbers from the artefacts, 0
mismatches, and reports the 2 that have no artefact rather than skipping them.

Still not done: no browser or node here, so the page has never been rendered and the
palette validator has never run. Verification remains static.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
MSG
  git log --oneline -1
  git -c credential.helper="store --file=$HOME/.git-credentials-github" \
      push origin main 2>&1 | sed -E 's#//[^@]*@#//***@#g'
  echo "push exit ${PIPESTATUS[0]}"
} 2>&1 | tee logs/98_push_report.live.log
